    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.8,
    "explanation": "To the rider and to the driver: the $4.00 cancellation fee is refunded to you in full, and the driver is paid $2.00 by the platform — not by the rider — as a pin-ambiguity goodwill payment. Nothing here is a finding of dishonesty against either of you.\n\nWHAT HAPPENED. On 28 July the driver accepted at 15:03:30, tapped 'arrived' at 15:12:05 and cancelled at 15:18:40 — a 6.6-minute hold. The driver's GPS trace shows his closest approach to the Lobby L pin was 284.95 m; he was holding at the HarbourFront kerb. The rider's own device sat between 7.57 m and 22.50 m of the pin on all 31 of her fixes, so she was at the pin throughout. The chat log holds only two SYSTEM notifications and no sub-location (no block, entrance, tower or bay) from either party. This is the wrong-face-of-the-same-venue case, not a rider no-show.\n\nWHY THE FEE CANNOT STAND. POL-NS-01 requires all four of its conditions. Limb (d) fails on the driver's own record: the cancellation reason code is DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE, which the clause excludes and treats as the driver's admission that he could not find the rider. Limb (b) also fails: the driver's qualifying in-radius fix count is 0 against the 120 m LARGE_VENUE arrival radius, his closest approach being 284.95 m. POL-NS-01 itself directs such a trip to POL-NS-03, which decides it.\n\nPOL-NS-03. The driver was stationary at about 285 m from the pin — outside the 120 m arrival radius but inside the 400 m ceiling that is the whole test — for the 300-second LARGE_VENUE minimum (22 fixes span the ~400 s dwell; wait_time_min 6.6). On those facts the cancellation fee is refunded to the rider in full. Fault is then allocated from the chat log for compensation only: with neither side naming a sub-location and 4 registered pickup points at this LARGE_VENUE zone, limb (ii) attributes the mislocation to pin ambiguity rather than to either party, and the driver receives a platform-funded goodwill of 50 percent of the fee — $2.00 of the $4.00 — charged to the platform and never recovered from the rider.\n\nCLAIMS ANSWERED. POL-NS-04 does not open (both sides agree): limb (a) needs a rider locating or coordinating message in the chat window, and the log contains none, so the clause cannot strip the driver of cost-sharing and the allocation stays with POL-NS-03. POL-NS-05 does not fire: the arrival marker sits at 284.95 m, inside the clause's 300 m line, and the stationary fixes are logged at 0.0 km/h, so no false-arrival event is recorded and no POL-NS-05(ii) referral is entered; the clause's own closing sentence sends this driver to POL-NS-03. POL-NS-06 (dwell-shortfall) is not relied on: the referee discarded the shortfall claims (RIDER and DRIVER) and the driver's 'for completeness' claim for failing to disclose the impairment of the artifacts they cited, and in any event the refund follows from POL-NS-03.\n\nTHE MONEY. The brief's fare_breakdown shows cancellation_fee $4.00, total_charged $4.00, payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd 0.0. That figure reconciles with the fee schedule — the greater of the LARGE_VENUE zone-class fee ($4.00) and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee ($4.00) — so there is no POL-NS-08(d) fare defect. Goodwill is 50 percent of $4.00 = $2.00. The refund and the goodwill are independent and are never netted.\n\nWEIGHT AND CONFIDENCE. The deciding facts rest on EV-TRIP-00206, EV-CHAT-00206 and EV-FARE-00206 at weight 1.0, and on EV-GPS-00206 at weight 0.8, impaired with issue LOW_SAMPLE_RATE (median sampling 18 s against a nominal 10 s, largest single interval 26 s, 52 fixes, gaps empty, rider track present). That tag does not meet any limb of POL-NS-08(a)–(d) — no gap over 120 s, more than 6 fixes in the window, rider_track present, no clock skew and a reconciled fare — so it is a confidence discount only. The 284.95 m closest-approach figure and the rider-presence figures survive the 0.8 discount and carry the outcome. Confidence is therefore capped at 0.80 and no adverse finding rests on either party's rating, account age, lifetime trips, cancellation rate or prior counters.\n\nNO ESCALATION, NO REFERRAL. None of POL-NS-09's triggers applies: confidence 0.80 is above the 0.70 floor; no two admissible artifacts contradict each other on arrival, dwell or rider presence (the 285 m stationary hold and the 6.6-minute wait agree); disputes_with_counterparty_90d is 0 on both profiles; rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 0; the POL-NS-07 anti-farming test does not trip (no_show_terminations_30d of 1 is below 4 and 1/187 = 0.005 is below 0.08); and no deciding fact rests solely on an artifact impaired under POL-NS-08(a)–(d). The case is decided on the money today rather than held. No clause produces a referral: POL-NS-05(ii) is not engaged because no false marker was shown."
  },
  "discarded_claims": [
