    "confidence": 0.8,
    "explanation": "To the rider and to the driver. Outcome: the $4.00 cancellation fee is refunded in full to the rider, and the driver receives a platform-funded goodwill payment of $2.00. These two figures are independent and are never netted: the $4.00 goes back to the rider, the $2.00 is paid by the platform, and neither party funds the other.\n\nWhy the fee does not stand. The trip record (EV-TRIP-00206) shows the trip terminated by the driver at 15:18:40 with cancellation_reason_code DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE. POL-NS-01(d) recognises only RIDER_NO_SHOW, RIDER_UNREACHABLE and EXCESSIVE_WAIT, and the clause itself directs a DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE trip to be decided under POL-NS-03, so the baseline no-show charge cannot be made out. The arrival test fails too: for a LARGE_VENUE pickup the arrival radius is 120 m, and the driver's trace (EV-GPS-00206) contains no qualifying fix inside it — his closest recorded approach to the pin was 284.95 m. Under POL-NS-02 that is a failure of POL-NS-01(b) and a full refund of the fee.\n\nWhy the driver still receives something. The same trace shows the driver stationary at roughly 285 m from the pin — outside the 120 m arrival radius but inside POL-NS-03's 400 m ceiling — across the waiting period: arrival 15:12:05 to cancellation 15:18:40, about 395 seconds, against the 300-second LARGE_VENUE minimum (trip record wait_time 6.6 min), with his stationary fixes logged at 0 km/h. That is the POL-NS-03 case. Fault is then allocated from the chat log (EV-CHAT-00206): it holds only two SYSTEM notifications and neither party named a block, entrance, tower or bay, while the trip record shows 4 registered pickup points at this venue. On POL-NS-03(ii) the mislocation is therefore pin ambiguity rather than party fault, and the driver is entitled to a platform-funded goodwill payment of 50 percent of the cancellation fee — $2.00 of the $4.00 — charged to the platform and never recovered from the rider.\n\nAmounts used. The $4.00 is the entire contested sum (EV-FARE-00206: cancellation_fee 4.00, total_charged 4.00, payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00), and it reconciles with the fee schedule — the greater of the LARGE_VENUE zone-class fee ($4.00) and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee ($4.00) — so there is no POL-NS-08(d) fare defect.\n\nEvidence weight. EV-GPS-00206 is IMPAIRED at weight_multiplier 0.8, issue code LOW_SAMPLE_RATE. That tag concerns sampling cadence only: 52 fixes span the window, the largest interval is 26 s, there is no gap over 120 s and the rider track is present, so it meets none of POL-NS-08 limbs (a) to (d) and the position finding survives the discount at full value. Because the deciding position fact is carried by this artifact at 0.8, my confidence is capped at 0.8 under POL-GEN-02(2); that is above the 0.70 floor, so the case is decided on the merits and is not escalated.\n\nClaims, answered together. The rider's claims that POL-NS-01(d) fails and that the fee is refunded under POL-NS-02 and POL-NS-03 are accepted, and the driver's concession to the same effect is accepted. The rider's and driver's POL-NS-03(ii) claims for $2.00 platform-funded goodwill are accepted, and the driver's point that this goodwill is not a POL-NS-07 payout and is never netted against the rider's refund is accepted. The rider's note that POL-NS-04 is not pressed is accepted: the chat log contains no rider locating message, so limb (a) does not open and that clause is not relied on. The driver's POL-NS-05 point is accepted: the arrival marker is not false — the minimum recorded distance of 284.95 m sits inside the 300 m line and the stationary fixes are 0 km/h — so no false-arrival record under POL-NS-05(ii) arises. The rider's and driver's rider-presence points are accepted and consistent (all 31 rider fixes stationary, 7.57 m to 22.50 m from the pin, inside the 150 m LARGE_VENUE rider radius), though POL-NS-03's test rests on the driver's position. Finally, the no-escalation points on both sides are accepted: rider no_show_disputes_30d is 0, both disputes_with_counterparty_90d are 0, and driver no_show_terminations_30d is 1 against completed_trips_30d of 187 (rate 0.005), so neither POL-NS-09(c) nor (d) fires and no POL-NS-07 anti-farming withholding arises. No clause produces a referral, so the referrals list is empty."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
